ll there's about a hundred and  thirty thousand interactions between  proteins computers feel accurately that  they have catalogued many of those which  is referred to as the human interactome  and at the moment there are over 33,000  unique ones protein to protein  interactions that have been identified  by various means using that computerized  data one then goes on to form various  interactions with the hope that we could  trap some of our genes in those networks  which would give us an idea at what's  going on so far in looking at the  network analysis we have had some  interesting results three of the  pathways carrying some of the genes are  involved in information and three of the  genetic variants that we've identified  shown on this slide one of them as you  can see is interleukin 6  are involved in those bit of bollocks  pathways we've strongly indicate that  inflammation is one of the means whereby  some of these particular risk bearings  mediate their risk when you put this  together what you're looking at here  inside the big circle is the normal  pathway for synthesizing cholesterol  then outside of the circle you had the  Interlochen stat and you had PDF which  is platelet derived growth factor those  genes have been shown to increase the  risk of coronary disease and they  mediate in different ways inflammation  but also what you see here that both  cholesterol and these other genes  interact true Kappa beta to have certain  effects on both the inflammatory pathway  as well as cholesterol so I think the  data is highly suggestive at this moment  that information is part of the pathway  which certainly people have postulated  for decades and this seems to be in  keeping and supportive of the concept we  know that atherosclerosis develops as a  result of an inflammatory process in  part mediated by cholesterol and now I  think you can see these genetic variants  predisposed for greater information in  these pathways and so we are expecting  that in the